ExitQueue::initialize(address _admin)
├── Given _admin is zero address
│   └── It should revert with ExitQueueZeroAddress
├── Given valid parameters
│   ├── It should set currentBatchId to 1
│   ├── It should grant ADMIN_ROLE to _admin
│   └── It should report version "1.0.0"
└── Given already initialized
    └── It should revert (InvalidInitialization)

ExitQueue::DEPLOYER_ROLE lifecycle (test_DeployerRole_CannotBeGranted_RenounceFreezesRoleGrants)
├── Given DEPLOYER_ROLE has not been renounced
│   ├── It should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount(admin, DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE) when granting DEPLOYER_ROLE
│   └── It should allow the deployer to grant AMM_ROLE
└── Given the deployer renounced DEPLOYER_ROLE
    ├── It should remove DEPLOYER_ROLE from the deployer
    ├── It should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount(admin, DEPLOYER_ROLE) when granting AMM_ROLE
    └── It should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount(admin, DEPLOYER_ROLE) when granting CONTROLLER_ROLE

ExitQueue::Access Control
├── Given caller has AMM_ROLE
│   ├── It should allow pushRequest (returns currentBatchId)
│   ├── It should allow pullRequest (after pricing)
│   └── It should allow closeRequest
├── Given caller has CONTROLLER_ROLE
│   └── It should allow priceBatch (when not paused)
└── Given caller is unauthorized
    ├── It should revert on pushRequest
    ├── It should revert on pullRequest
    ├── It should revert on priceBatch
    └── It should revert on closeRequest

ExitQueue::batchInfo(uint256 _batchId)
├── Given batch exists but not priced
│   ├── It should return canBeProcessed=false
│   ├── It should return finalEvePrice=0
│   ├── It should return totalTokensToBurn (sum of all requests)
│   ├── It should return createdAt (timestamp when batch was created)
│   └── It should return pricedAt=0
└── Given batch exists and is priced
    ├── It should return canBeProcessed=true
    ├── It should return finalEvePrice (set by priceBatch)
    ├── It should return totalTokensToBurn
    ├── It should return createdAt (timestamp when batch was created, not when priced)
    └── It should return pricedAt (timestamp when priceBatch was called)

ExitQueue::requestInfo(uint256 _batchId, address _user)
├── Given request does not exist
│   └── It should return default values (processed=false, closedDueToSlippage=false, all other fields=0)
└── Given request exists and not processed
    ├── It should return processed=false
    ├── It should return closedDueToSlippage=false
    ├── It should return evePriceAtRequestTime (from pushRequest)
    ├── It should return tokensToBurn (from pushRequest)
    └── It should return priceTolerance (from pushRequest)

ExitQueue::requestCanBeClosed(uint256 _batchId, address _user)
├── Given batch does not exist
│   └── It should return false
├── Given user is not in batch
│   └── It should return false
├── Given request is already processed
│   └── It should return false
├── Given request exists, batch not priced
│   └── It should return true (user can cancel before pricing)
├── Given request exists, batch priced, within MAX_BATCH_PROCESSING_TIME
│   └── It should return false (must be pulled, cannot close)
├── Given request exists, batch priced, at exactly MAX_BATCH_PROCESSING_TIME
│   └── It should return false (upper bound exclusive)
└── Given request exists, batch priced, MAX_BATCH_PROCESSING_TIME exceeded
    └── It should return true (escape hatch available)

ExitQueue::unprocessedUsersCount(uint256 _batchId)
└── Given batch exists with requests
    ├── It should return count of unprocessed users
    └── It should return 0 once all requests are pulled or closed

ExitQueue::unprocessedUsers(uint256 _batchId)
└── Given batch exists with requests
    └── It should return array of all unprocessed user addresses

ExitQueue::unprocessedUsers(uint256 _batchId, uint256 _startIndex, uint256 _endIndex)
├── Given range is invalid (startIndex >= endIndex or endIndex > length)
│   └── It should revert with ExitQueueInvalidRange
└── Given range is valid
    └── It should return array of users in the specified range

ExitQueue::pushRequest(address _user, uint256 _evePriceAtRequestTime, uint256 _tokensToBurn, uint256 _priceTolerance)
├── Given caller does not have AMM_ROLE
│   └── It should revert (AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount)
└── Given caller has AMM_ROLE
    ├── When user already has request in current batch
    │   └── It should revert with ExitQueueRequestAlreadyInBatch
    ├── When contract is paused
    │   └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
    ├── When valid parameters
    │   ├── It should store request info (price, tokens, tolerance)
    │   ├── It should add user to unprocessedUsers set
    │   ├── It should update batch.totalTokensToBurn
    │   ├── It should emit RequestPushed event
    │   └── It should return currentBatchId
    ├── When multiple distinct users push
    │   └── It should track each user independently (unprocessedUsers count grows)
    └── When tokensToBurn is zero
        └── It should still succeed (batch totalTokensToBurn stays 0)

ExitQueue::priceBatch(uint256 _evePrice)
├── Given caller is not the registered Controller
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientInvalidCaller
├── Given caller is the registered Controller
│   ├── When contract is paused
│   │   └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
│   ├── When _evePrice is zero
│   │   └── It should revert with ExitQueueZeroPrice
│   ├── When current batch is empty (no requests)
│   │   └── It should revert with ExitQueueBatchIsEmpty
│   └── When current batch has requests
│       ├── It should set batch.finalEvePrice to _evePrice
│       ├── It should set batch.canBeProcessed to true
│       ├── It should set batch.pricedAt to block.timestamp
│       ├── It should increment currentBatchId
│       └── It should emit BatchPriced event
└── Given reentrancy attempt
    └── It should revert (if reentrancy guard is added)

ExitQueue::pullRequest(uint256 _batchId, address _user)
├── Given caller does not have AMM_ROLE
│   └── It should revert (AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount)
└── Given caller has AMM_ROLE
    ├── When batch is not priced (canBeProcessed=false)
    │   └── It should revert with ExitQueueBatchCannotBeProcessed
    ├── When request is already processed
    │   └── It should revert with ExitQueueRequestAlreadyProcessed
    ├── When user is not in batch
    │   └── It should revert with ExitQueueRequestNotInBatch
    ├── When contract is paused
    │   └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
    ├── When price slippage exceeds tolerance
    │   ├── It should set request.closedDueToSlippage=true
    │   ├── It should set request.processed=true
    │   ├── It should remove user from unprocessedUsers
    │   ├── It should update batch.totalTokensToBurn (subtract tokens)
    │   └── It should emit RequestPulled event (isWithinTolerance=false)
    ├── When price is within tolerance
    │   ├── It should set request.processed=true
    │   ├── It should set request.closedDueToSlippage=false
    │   ├── It should remove user from unprocessedUsers
    │   ├── It should update batch.totalTokensToBurn (subtract tokens)
    │   └── It should emit RequestPulled event (isWithinTolerance=true)
    └── When price is exactly at tolerance boundary
        ├── It should NOT set closedDueToSlippage (price is not LESS than threshold)
        └── It should process normally

ExitQueue::closeRequest(uint256 _batchId, address _user) returns (bool _viaEscapeHatch)
├── Given caller does not have AMM_ROLE
│   └── It should revert (AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount)
└── Given caller has AMM_ROLE
    ├── When request is already processed
    │   └── It should revert with ExitQueueRequestAlreadyProcessed
    ├── When user is not in batch
    │   └── It should revert with ExitQueueRequestNotInBatch
    ├── When batch is priced and within MAX_BATCH_PROCESSING_TIME
    │   ├── It should revert with ExitQueueRequestCannotBeClosed
    │   └── It should revert for every user in the batch
    ├── When batch is priced at exactly MAX_BATCH_PROCESSING_TIME
    │   └── It should revert with ExitQueueRequestCannotBeClosed (upper bound exclusive)
    ├── When batch is priced but MAX_BATCH_PROCESSING_TIME exceeded
    │   ├── It should allow close (escape hatch for unprocessed requests)
    │   ├── It should emit RequestClosed event with viaEscapeHatch=true
    │   ├── It should completely remove request from batch (request resets to defaults)
    │   ├── It should remove user from unprocessedUsers
    │   └── It should allow all users in batch to close
    ├── When valid parameters (batch not priced)
    │   ├── It should completely remove request from batch (delete)
    │   ├── It should remove user from unprocessedUsers
    │   ├── It should update batch.totalTokensToBurn (subtract tokens)
    │   ├── It should emit RequestClosed event with viaEscapeHatch=false
    │   └── It should allow user to re-request in same batch
    └── When contract is paused
        └── It should still succeed (works when paused for emergency withdrawal)

ExitQueue::pause()
├── Given caller has neither ADMIN_ROLE nor SECURITY_ROLE on Registry
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientCallerHasNoneOfRoles
├── Given caller has SECURITY_ROLE on Registry
│   └── It should pause the contract immediately (no timelock)
├── Given caller has ADMIN_ROLE on Registry
│   ├── When contract is not paused
│   │   ├── It should pause the contract
│   │   └── It should emit Paused event
│   └── When contract is already paused
│       └── It should revert with EnforcedPause

ExitQueue::unpause()
├── Given caller has ADMIN_ROLE
│   └── It should unpause the contract (paused() == false)
└── Given caller is unauthorized
    └── It should revert (AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount)

ExitQueue::Scenarios
├── Multiple batches (test_MultipleBatches)
│   ├── It should assign batchId 1 to the first batch and batchId 2 to the next
│   ├── It should increment currentBatchId after pricing
│   └── It should keep batches independent (first priced/processable, second unpriced)
├── Process multiple requests in a batch (test_ProcessMultipleRequestsInBatch)
│   ├── It should pull every request after pricing
│   ├── It should drive unprocessedUsersCount to 0
│   └── It should mark every request processed
├── Mix of close and pull (test_MixOfCloseAndPull)
│   ├── It should close some requests before pricing
│   ├── It should pull the remaining request after pricing
│   └── It should drive unprocessedUsersCount to 0
├── Zero tokensToBurn (test_ZeroTokensToBurn)
│   └── It should keep batch.totalTokensToBurn at 0
└── Zero price tolerance (test_ZeroPriceTolerance)
    └── It should mark any price drop as closedDueToSlippage=true (processed=true)

ExitQueue::pause behavior
├── Given contract is paused
│   ├── pushRequest should revert with EnforcedPause
│   ├── pullRequest should revert with EnforcedPause
│   ├── priceBatch should revert with EnforcedPause
│   └── closeRequest should still succeed (emergency withdrawal)
└── Given contract is unpaused again
    ├── pushRequest should work
    ├── pullRequest should work (after pricing)
    └── priceBatch should work
